Origin: from 5641;
Meaning: properly, a concealer, i.e. a covert
KJV renders: secret(-ly, place).

H4566.strongs:
Origin: from 5647;
Meaning: an act
KJV renders: work.

H4567.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 4566;
Meaning: an act
KJV renders: work.

H4568.strongs:
Origin: from 5666;
Meaning: properly, compact (part of soil), i.e. loam
KJV renders: clay.

H4569.strongs:
Origin: or feminine מַעֲבָרָה; from 5674;
Meaning: a crossing-place (of a river, a ford; of a mountain, a pass); abstractly, a transit, i.e. (figuratively) overwhelming
KJV renders: ford, place where...pass, passage.

H4570.strongs:
Origin: or feminine מַעְגָּלָה; from the same as 5696;
Meaning: a track (literally or figuratively); also a rampart (as circular)
KJV renders: going, path, trench, way(-side).

H4571.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to waver
KJV renders: make to shake, slide, slip.

H4572.strongs:
Origin: from 5710; ornamental;
Meaning: Maadai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Maadai.

H4573.strongs:
Origin: from 5710 and 3050; ornament of Jah;
Meaning: Maadjah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Maadiah. Compare 4153.

H4574.strongs:
Origin: or (feminine) מַעֲדַנָּה; from 5727;
Meaning: a delicacy or (abstractly) pleasure (adverbially, cheerfully)
KJV renders: dainty, delicately, delight.

H4575.strongs:
Origin: by transitive from 6029;
Meaning: a bond, i.e. group
KJV renders: influence.

H4576.strongs:
Origin: from 5737;
Meaning: a (weeding) hoe
KJV renders: mattock.

H4577.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) or מְעָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to 4578;
Meaning: only in plural the bowels
KJV renders: belly.

H4578.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root probably meaning to be soft;
Meaning: used only in plural the intestines, or (collectively) the abdomen, figuratively, sympathy; by implication, a vest; by extension the stomach, the uterus (or of men, the seat of generation), the heart (figuratively)
KJV renders: belly, bowels, × heart, womb.

H4579.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 4578;
Meaning: the belly, i.e. (figuratively) interior
KJV renders: gravel.

H4581.strongs:
Origin: (also מָעוּז ); or מָעֹז (also מָעֻז; from 5810;
Meaning: a fortified place; figuratively, a defence
KJV renders: force, fort(-ress), rock, strength(-en), (× most) strong (hold).

H4582.strongs:
Origin: from 4600; oppressed;
Meaning: Maok, a Philistine
KJV renders: Maoch.

H4583.strongs:
Origin: or מָעִין; (1 Chronicles 4:41), from the same as 5772;
Meaning: an abode, of God (the Tabernacle or the Temple), men (their home) or animals (their lair); hence, a retreat (asylum)
KJV renders: den, dwelling((-) place), habitation.

H4584.strongs:
Origin: the same as 4583; a residence;
Meaning: Maon, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Maon, Maonites. Compare 1010, 4586.

H4586.strongs:
Origin: or מְעִינִי; probably patrial from 4584;
Meaning: a Meunite, or inhabitant of Maon (only in plural)
KJV renders: Mehunim(-s), Meunim.

H4587.strongs:
Origin: plural of 4585; habitative;
Meaning: Meonothai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Meonothai.

H4588.strongs:
Origin: from 5774 in the sense of covering with shade (compare 4155);
Meaning: darkness
KJV renders: dimness.

H4589.strongs:
Origin: from 5783;
Meaning: nakedness, i.e. (in plural) the pudenda
KJV renders: nakedness.

H4590.strongs:
Origin: or מַעַזְיָהוּ; probably from 5756 (in the sense of protection) and 3050; rescue of Jah;
Meaning: Maazjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Maaziah.

H4591.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to pare off, i.e. lessen; intransitively, to be (or causatively, to make) small or few (or figuratively, ineffective)
KJV renders: suffer to decrease, diminish, (be, × borrow a, give, make) few (in number, -ness), gather least (little), be (seem) little, (× give the) less, be minished, bring to nothing.

H4592.strongs:
Origin: or מְעָט; from 4591;
Meaning: a little or few (often adverbial or comparative)
KJV renders: almost (some, very) few(-er, -est), lightly, little (while), (very) small (matter, thing), some, soon, × very.

H4593.strongs:
Origin: passive adjective of 4591;
Meaning: thinned (as to the edge), i.e. sharp
KJV renders: wrapped up.

H4594.strongs:
Origin: from 5844;
Meaning: a vestment
KJV renders: garment.

H4595.strongs:
Origin: from 5848;
Meaning: a cloak
KJV renders: mantle.

H4597.strongs:
Origin: probably from 4578; sympathetic;
Meaning: Maai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Maai.

H4598.strongs:
Origin: from 4603 in the sense of covering;
Meaning: a robe (i.e. upper and outer garment)
KJV renders: cloke, coat, mantle, robe.

H4599.strongs:
Origin: or מַעְיְנוֹ; (Psalm 114:8), or (feminine) מַעְיָנָה; from 5869 (as a denominative in the sense of a spring);
Meaning: a fountain (also collectively), figuratively, a source (of satisfaction)
KJV renders: fountain, spring, well.
